From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:52:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deps: Update mozjs to the latest version

There were no breaking changes in the API, so we can just update
to the latest version. This pull in upstream SpiderMonkey fixes

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 13f4e0d2fe85ef8c93e9e88070f7ab6fecb653c2)

----

Fork note: backported onto Servo v0.6.0 for the ohos-v0.6 branch. A commit of upstream's release/v0.6 branch after v0.6.0, taken unchanged so that the next v0.6.x release supersedes it. It moves mozjs from 0.26.3 to 0.26.14 (SpiderMonkey 153.3 to 153.6), the version of servo-quickjs's main branch, so that ohos-v0.6 pins that branch as ohos-main does: Cargo applies the shim's `[patch]` only to the mozjs version that Cargo.toml requires. From here on the pin of `script: Run debugger.js on QuickJS` (servo-quickjs 6ac4a17, 0.26.14) applies again, so `--js-engine quickjs` takes the shim (`./mach check --js-engine quickjs` passes here). `cargo update -p mozjs --precise 0.26.14` on this stack gives upstream's Cargo.lock change exactly.

Validation: On the final stack, at its tip: `./mach test-tidy` (including cargo-deny), `./mach test-scripts`, `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (checked-release, -D warnings, crown built for Rust 1.97.1), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` with and without `--doc`, and the OpenHarmony checked-release builds of both flavors with -D warnings, which make signed HAPs, pass; release builds of it with both engines ran the whole WPT suite. `./mach check --js-engine quickjs` passes at this commit, with mozjs 0.26.14 from servo-quickjs 6ac4a17 and no `[[patch.unused]]`. Its full WPT runs (57,523 tests each): with SpiderMonkey, 57,421 ran as expected (57,415 on plain v0.6.0), and of the 99 tests that differed from plain v0.6.0's run, two reruns on each side and five more of the rest leave no consistent difference; with QuickJS, 57,419 as expected, and none of the 104 others had results only with QuickJS in three reruns with each engine. On a DAYU200 with OpenHarmony 7.0, the stack's QuickJS headless checked-release executable ran /infrastructure, /css/css-backgrounds and /webstorage through `mach test-wpt --ohos` (1,098 tests in 31 minutes) without a crash in css-backgrounds; one webstorage quota test was reported crashed, as these tests crash under load on the host too.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit 13f4e0d2fe8 without changes, checked that `cargo update -p mozjs --precise 0.26.14` gives the same Cargo.lock, and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
